<figure class="pa-figure" aria-labelledby="pa-process-title">
 <figcaption id="pa-process-title"><span class="pa-number">Figure 1</span> <strong>One connection, one backend</strong></figcaption>
 <div class="pa-drawing">
  <div class="pa-two pa-client-pair"><div class="pa-box"><span class="pa-label">Shop application</span><b>Connection A</b><small>SELECT price … P7</small></div><div class="pa-box"><span class="pa-label">Report application</span><b>Connection B</b><small>A separate SQL conversation</small></div></div>
  <div class="pa-arrow">↓ queries · ↑ rows, command results and errors</div>
  <div class="pa-server"><span class="pa-label">One PostgreSQL server instance</span><div class="pa-supervisor">Supervisor process · accepts new connections, starts backends</div><div class="pa-two"><div class="pa-box pa-active"><span class="pa-label">Backend A · process</span><b>Parse/analyse → rewrite → plan → execute</b><small>Work inside one backend</small></div><div class="pa-box"><span class="pa-label">Backend B · process</span><b>Its own query and transaction state</b><small>Can use the same cached pages</small></div></div><div class="pa-arrow">↓ shared access ↓</div><div class="pa-box"><span class="pa-label">Shared memory</span><b>Shared buffers · cached table and index pages</b><small>Also shared coordination and WAL buffers</small></div><div class="pa-arrow">↓ page reads and later writes ↓</div><div class="pa-box"><span class="pa-label">Server storage</span><b>Heap files · index files · WAL</b></div></div>
 </div>
 <p class="pa-caption">A process map for two direct server connections, with background processes added later. A pool may lend these connections to different requests. The supervisor is involved in establishing a connection; it does not forward each query between the client and its backend.</p>
</figure>
